    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In this podcast, we examine the stereotypes of the Asian-American identity and delicacy of the ballerina through a rendition of the 80's teen film, The Breakfast Club. Three PWR2 students are placed in detention one Saturday and are forced to create a podcast as punishment. Along the way, each student describes her experiences with stereotypes and provides further insight on her respective theme. In the end, they realize that everyone, to some degree, is a nerd, skinnie-minnie, and stoner at heart.",
            "type": "abstract",
